## Summary for AI Assistants (Claude, Copilot)

When helping with this project:
1. **Follow Java conventions** - PascalCase classes, camelCase methods
2. **Use Spring Boot patterns** - @Service, @Repository, @Controller
3. **Implement proper error handling** - Custom exceptions, @ControllerAdvice
4. **Write tests** - Unit tests with Mockito, integration tests with @SpringBootTest
5. **Security first** - Use Spring Security, hash passwords, validate input
6. **Database migrations** - Use Flyway, never modify committed migrations
7. **SE358 compliance** - Follow team rules, create log files, proper PR descriptions
8. **Code quality** - 80%+ test coverage, meaningful names, documented code
9. **Performance** - Pagination, avoid N+1 queries, use caching when appropriate
10. **Documentation** - JSDoc for public methods, clear commit messages, up-to-date READMEs
